{"status":"Error","code":"InvalidParameter","error":"The Costing domain is turned off for this company. Turn it on from Inventory Setup.","nextStep":"Ask an administrator with the Inv. Posting Gate permission set to turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page. Data.Records.Set cannot change this setup.","hint":"For usage details, call the \"Help.Implementation.Get\" message type with subject \"Inventory.Cost.Update\". Always read the help before calling a message type."}

--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "subject": {
      "use": "optional",
      "forms": [
        "itemNo",
        "systemId"
      ],
      "description": "Exactly one item; subject precedes data identifiers."
    },
    "dataRequired": true,
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json"
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "subject",
      "form": "guid",
      "description": "The SystemId of the Item."
    },
    {
      "source": "subject",
      "form": "item no.",
      "description": "The No. of the Item."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.itemNo",
      "form": "item no.",
      "description": "The No. of the Item; used when subject is empty."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.itemId, data.id, data.systemId, data.recordSystemId",
      "form": "guid",
      "description": "The SystemId of the Item; any one of the four keys."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.tableView",
      "form": "table view",
      "description": "An Item table view that selects the item it must select exactly one item."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "itemNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The No. of the Item; used when subject is empty."
    },
    {
      "name": "itemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The SystemId of the Item; used after the subject and itemNo."
    },
    {
      "name": "id",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Alias for the Item SystemId."
    },
    {
      "name": "systemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Alias for the Item SystemId."
    },
    {
      "name": "recordSystemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Alias for the Item SystemId."
    },
    {
      "name": "tableView",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "An Item table view; it must select exactly one item."
    },
    {
      "name": "unitCost",
      "type": "number",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The new Unit Cost of the item, as a JSON number or an invariant decimal text such as 12.5."
    },
    {
      "name": "lastDirectCost",
      "type": "number",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The new Last Direct Cost of the item, as a JSON number or an invariant decimal text."
    },
    {
      "name": "standardCost",
      "type": "number",
      "required": false,
      "description": "The new Standard Cost of the item, as a JSON number or an invariant decimal text. Items with the Standard costing method are refused whatever you send."
    },
    {
      "name": "allowBlocked",
      "type": "boolean",
      "required": false,
      "description": "true permits changing a blocked item; default false."
    },
    {
      "name": "expectedCostingMethod",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Optional guard: the costing method the item must have, for example FIFO or Average; the comparison ignores case."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success."
      },
      {
        "name": "itemNo",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The No. of the updated Item."
      },
      {
        "name": "itemId",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The SystemId of the updated Item."
      },
      {
        "name": "costingMethod",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The costing method name of the item, for example FIFO or Average."
      },
      {
        "name": "before",
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The three card cost fields before the change.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "unitCost",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The Unit Cost of the item."
          },
          {
            "name": "lastDirectCost",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The Last Direct Cost of the item."
          },
          {
            "name": "standardCost",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The Standard Cost of the item."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "after",
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The same three card cost fields after the change.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "unitCost",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The Unit Cost of the item."
          },
          {
            "name": "lastDirectCost",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The Last Direct Cost of the item."
          },
          {
            "name": "standardCost",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The Standard Cost of the item."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "warnings",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "Always empty on a successful call."
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "when": "The subject, itemNo, SystemId key or tableView matches no item.",
      "fix": "Supply an existing item."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The caller has no write permission on items.",
      "fix": "Review the permissions of the caller."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "The Costing domain is turned off in Inventory Setup.",
      "fix": "Turn on the Costing domain in Inventory Setup."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "unitCost, lastDirectCost, standardCost or allowBlocked has the wrong format, or an item selection key is invalid.",
      "fix": "Use JSON numbers or invariant decimal text for the costs, JSON true or false for allowBlocked, and valid identifiers."
    },
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "when": "unitCost, lastDirectCost or standardCost is present but null or empty.",
      "fix": "Supply a numeric cost value or leave the key out."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "The refusal or validation text of Business Central.",
      "when": "No item is selected or several items match, none of the three cost keys is sent, the item is Standard-costed, or blocked without allowBlocked, expectedCostingMethod is not text or does not match, a cost field is restricted, or Business Central validation fails. The text is returned as it is, with code BusinessCentralError, and nothing is changed.",
      "fix": "Use Inventory.Revaluation.Post for Standard-costed items; otherwise correct the request."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "write",
    "writes": true,
    "posts": false,
    "changes": "Changes the unit cost, last direct cost and standard cost you send on one Item card. No revaluation, no value entries and no ledger entries are created. All checks run before the first field is changed, and a failure changes nothing. Business Central commits the change when the call finishes.",
    "idempotent": true,
    "permissionSet": "Bifrost Full Access",
    "preconditions": [
      "Exactly one Item selected.",
      "Non-Standard costing method.",
      "Native Item write access and each supplied field permission.",
      "Costing domain and normal licensed dispatch."
    ]
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Cost.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Use it to read the current costs before or after the update; it changes nothing."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Revaluation.Post",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Use it to change the value of Standard-costed items, which this type refuses."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Price.Update",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Use it to change the unit price; this type never changes prices."
    }
  ],
  "workflow": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Cost.Get",
        "purpose": "Read the current costs and the costing method of the item."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Cost.Update",
        "purpose": "Change the card cost fields of a non-Standard item."
      }
    ]
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Update the unit cost and last direct cost of item 1000, guarded by its costing method",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.Cost.Update",
        "data": {
          "itemNo": "1000",
          "unitCost": 12,
          "lastDirectCost": 10,
          "expectedCostingMethod": "FIFO"
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "itemNo": "1000",
        "itemId": "6f1c1d2e-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
        "costingMethod": "FIFO",
        "before": {
          "unitCost": 11,
          "lastDirectCost": 9,
          "standardCost": 0
        },
        "after": {
          "unitCost": 12,
          "lastDirectCost": 10,
          "standardCost": 0
        },
        "warnings": []
      }
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Writes current Item card costs through Validate. It does not revalue inventory or post ledger entries.",
  "notes": "Select exactly one item with the message subject, data.itemNo, an item SystemId key or data.tableView; several matches are refused. Send at least one of unitCost, lastDirectCost and standardCost. Standard-costed items are always refused; use Inventory.Revaluation.Post for them. A blocked item is refused unless allowBlocked is true, and expectedCostingMethod must match the costing method of the item when it is sent. All checks run before the first field is changed, so a refusal changes nothing; the fields are then validated and the item is saved in one step. before and after show the three cost fields around the change. Nothing is revalued or posted. In a chained Omit Commit call, the write remains in the caller transaction and a native failure propagates so the whole chain can roll back."
}

## Errors and warnings
An error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.
When a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.
Request values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.
Request values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `"1234.56"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.
Answers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.
Both success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.
`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {"type":"Memory.User.Set","strict":true,"data":{"memory":"test","memry":"typo"}} is refused.
`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.
Feature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.
A message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.
`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is "no concurrent lock on the same records"; `nextStep` is "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed." Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.
Codes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.
